# Accessibility — framework-agnostic

## Semantic HTML first
- `<button>` for actions, `<a href>` for navigation, `<dialog>` for modals.
- Never an interactive `<div>`. Outline pages with `<nav>` / `<main>` / `<header>` / `<footer>`.

## Keyboard
- Every interactive element reachable by Tab in document order.
- Visible focus styles. Match widget role (arrows in menus/tabs, Esc closes dialogs).
- Skip-link at the top of every layout.

## Focus management
- Modals trap focus; restore to trigger on close.
- Move focus to `<main>` / new heading after route changes.
- Live regions: `aria-live="polite"` (chat, score), `"assertive"` only for critical (errors, payment).
- Don't move focus on real-time updates.

## Forms
- `<label htmlFor>` always; placeholder is not a label.
- `<fieldset>` + `<legend>` for groups.
- Errors via `aria-describedby` + `role="alert"`.

## Images & media
- Meaningful `alt`; decorative use `alt=""`. Icon-only buttons → `aria-label`.
- Captions for video. No auto-play with sound without visible mute.

## Colour & motion
- Contrast ≥ 4.5:1 (3:1 for large/bold). Never colour alone for state.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`. Avoid flashes ≥ 3 Hz.

## Real-time gotchas
- Don't yank focus on incoming frames.
- Score updates: `aria-live="polite"` + `aria-atomic="true"`.

## Testing
- `@axe-core/playwright` on every E2E spec. Manual smoke with VoiceOver / NVDA.
